AU  - Kim, Yoonji
AU  - Kim, Jieun
AU  - Jeong, Yujin
AU  - Cho, Sung-Bae
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 64th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 1: Long Papers)
AB  - Consistent reasoning about 3D spatial relations across changing viewpoints is fundamental for Embodied AI agents operating in dynamic environments. While Large Vision-Language Models (LVLMs) have advanced multimodal perception, their ability to maintain spatial consistency across diverse perspectives remains underexplored. Existing benchmarks primarily assess spatial capabilities from a static, single-view, and egocentric perspective, failing to capture the dynamic nature of real-world spatial cognition.To address this gap, we introduce SCOPE (Spatial COnsistency across PErspectives and Viewpoints), a comprehensive benchmark designed to rigorously diagnose spatial reasoning capabilities. Grounded in human cognitive theories of dual spatial representations, SCOPE discretizes the 360^\circ field into multiview scenarios to systematically evaluate both allocentric and egocentric reasoning capabilities. Our dataset comprises 20.1K spatial VQA pairs derived from high-quality 3D environments. Through an extensive evaluation of 26 state-of-the-art LVLMs, we identify two fundamental limitations that prevent consistent spatial understanding across viewpoints.We hope SCOPE facilitates the diagnosis of spatial reasoning, serving as a stepping stone toward reliable embodied action.
